{
  "about": "Area in production (ha) and total volume produced (hl, non-marketable included) for each French PDO, from the customs' open data «Superficies et volumes en production par produit — Déclaration de récolte et de production 2024 (campagne 2024-2025)», DGDDI, extraction of 5 February 2025 (casier viticole informatisé). Licence Ouverte / Etalab 2.0. A PDO's products are summed under its name: its colours and styles, its alternative names («Brouilly ou Brouilly cru du Beaujolais»), its complementary geographical names and premiers crus («Côtes de Bordeaux Blaye», «Beaune premier cru»), and the wine declared as fit for it or meant for it («Vin apte Madiran», «Vin destiné à l'élaboration de Champagne»). Wine meant for spirits (Cognac, Armagnac, Fine Bordeaux) and confidential cells (secret statistique) are left out, so a PDO with a confidential product is a lower bound.",
  "campaign": "2024",
